  "problems": {
    "B461": "Plain commands rechecked cancellation only after handler execution. A run-event listener can cancel before entry, yet the handler mutates state; simultaneous registration removal can also replace the cancellation with a normal error result.",
    "B462": "Managed /plan content is steered as an unstamped user message. The actual PostgreSQL execution provider treats it as unverified history, losing the interactive input identity; missing required authority is not refused before mode selection."
  },
  "fixes": {
    "B461": "The cancellation cutoff applies after Session publication for every accepted command, before registration revalidation and handler entry.",
    "B462": "New text and attachment input is stamped by the captured execution provider before mode selection and delivery. Cancellation, provider replacement, service disposal and loss of the original Agent during the wait prevent both operations. Required managed authority cannot fall back to local execution."
  },
